│                               ││ +                                                               │
│                               ││ + # Baker Percentages, Explained                                │
│                               ││ +                                                               │
│                               ││ + Professional bakers rarely write a recipe as a list of        │
│                               ││   ingredient weights.                                           │
│                               ││ + They write it as a set of percentages of the flour weight, a  │
│                               ││   convention                                                    │
│                               ││ + called baker percentages. Flour is always one hundred         │
│                               ││   percent, and every                                            │
│                               ││ + other ingredient is measured against it, so a dough at        │
│                               ││   seventy percent                                               │
│                               ││ + hydration carries water equal to seven tenths of its flour.   │
│                               ││ +                                                               │
│                               ││ + ## Why bakers use it                                          │
